[§](#variant.Percentage)

### Percentage([u16](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u16.html))

Applies a percentage of the available space to the element

Converts the given percentage to a floating-point value and multiplies that with area. This value is rounded back to a integer as part of the layout split calculation.

**Note**: As this value only accepts a `u16`, certain percentages that cannot be represented exactly (e.g. 1/3) are not possible. You might want to use [`Constraint::Ratio`](../prelude/enum.Constraint.html#variant.Ratio "variant ratatui::prelude::Constraint::Ratio") or [`Constraint::Fill`](../prelude/enum.Constraint.html#variant.Fill "variant ratatui::prelude::Constraint::Fill") in such cases.

#### [§](#examples-4)Examples

`[Percentage(75), Fill(1)]`

```
┌────────────────────────────────────┐┌──────────┐
│                38 px               ││   12 px  │
└────────────────────────────────────┘└──────────┘
```

`[Percentage(50), Fill(1)]`

```
┌───────────────────────┐┌───────────────────────┐
│         25 px         ││         25 px         │
└───────────────────────┘└───────────────────────┘
```

[§](#variant.Ratio)

### Ratio([u32](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u32.html), [u32](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u32.html))

Applies a ratio of the available space to the element

Converts the given ratio to a floating-point value and multiplies that with area. This value is rounded back to a integer as part of the layout split calculation.

#### [§](#examples-5)Examples

`[Ratio(1, 2) ; 2]`

```
┌───────────────────────┐┌───────────────────────┐
│         25 px         ││         25 px         │
└───────────────────────┘└───────────────────────┘
```

`[Ratio(1, 4) ; 4]`

```
┌───────────┐┌──────────┐┌───────────┐┌──────────┐
│   13 px   ││   12 px  ││   13 px   ││   12 px  │
└───────────┘└──────────┘└───────────┘└──────────┘
```

[§](#variant.Fill)

### Fill([u16](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.u16.html))

Applies the scaling factor proportional to all other [`Constraint::Fill`](../prelude/enum.Constraint.html#variant.Fill "variant ratatui::prelude::Constraint::Fill") elements to fill excess space

The element will only expand or fill into excess available space, proportionally matching other [`Constraint::Fill`](../prelude/enum.Constraint.html#variant.Fill "variant ratatui::prelude::Constraint::Fill") elements while satisfying all other constraints.

#### [§](#examples-6)Examples

`[Fill(1), Fill(2), Fill(3)]`

```
┌──────┐┌───────────────┐┌───────────────────────┐
│ 8 px ││     17 px     ││         25 px         │
└──────┘└───────────────┘└───────────────────────┘
```

`[Fill(1), Percentage(50), Fill(1)]`

```
┌───────────┐┌───────────────────────┐┌──────────┐
│   13 px   ││         25 px         ││   12 px  │
└───────────┘└───────────────────────┘└──────────┘
```

